Cosmetic, no failure. Since karr #92 / ADR 0019 a `True` string in an
unencrypted YAML slot carps, and two existing tests encrypt exactly that
without capturing warnings, so `prove -lr t/` prints the full warning text
several times:

  t/31-negative-zero-integer-cache.t line 420  (the karr #86 acceptance list)
  t/33-guard-answers-from-the-token.t line 68  (guard_asked, several leaves)

Both files pass and both assert the right thing - "is still written", not "says
nothing", so their claims are unaffected. What is wrong is only the output: a
500-character warning in the middle of a green run reads like a defect.

Fix is a local $SIG{__WARN__} in each file helper (t/33 guard_asked already
wraps the guard; t/31 loop does not capture anything). Left alone deliberately
by the wire lane, which was told not to touch t/ beyond the test belonging to
its own change - t/35-string-go-reads-as-boolean.t. Test lane.
